---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import TextBlock from '../components/TextBlock.astro';
import LinkCard from '../components/LinkCard.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const footerLinks = [
  { label: 'EEC', href: '/eec/' },
  { label: 'Behavioral Emails', href: '/behavioral-emails/' },
  { label: 'LinkedIn', href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrew-malashenko/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="First Action Fix — Educational Email Courses for AI SaaS"
  description="I build Educational Email Courses for AI SaaS companies. The step between stranger and trial user that most funnels don't have."
  theme="main"
  activePage="about"
>

  <!-- ===== HERO ===== -->
  <Hero
    headline="I build Educational Email Courses for AI SaaS companies."
    subheadline="The step between &ldquo;stranger&rdquo; and &ldquo;trial user&rdquo; that most funnels don&rsquo;t have. I create it."
    ctaText="Book a Free Diagnostic →"
    ctaLink="https://calendly.com/follow_action/30min"
  />

  <!-- ===== WHAT AN EEC DOES ===== -->
  <TextBlock heading="What an EEC Does" alt>
    <p>Most AI SaaS companies have two states in their funnel: stranger and trial user. Nothing in between.</p>
    <p>Their funnel looks like this:</p>
    <p class="funnel-flow">Blog/ad → landing page → trial signup → onboarding emails → paid</p>
    <p>That works for the small percentage of visitors ready to commit to a trial. The rest leave. They were interested, just not ready.</p>
    <p>An Educational Email Course creates a middle state: <strong>educated subscriber</strong>.</p>
    <p class="funnel-flow">Blog/ad → EEC signup (lower commitment) → 5-7 days of education → trial CTA → onboarding → paid</p>
    <a href="/eec/" class="btn btn--outline mt-3">Learn more about EECs →</a>
  </TextBlock>

  <!-- ===== WHO THIS IS FOR ===== -->
  <TextBlock heading="Who This Is For">
    <p>AI SaaS companies, Seed to Series A. Developer tools. API-first AI products. Vertical and agentic AI SaaS.</p>
    <p>The common pattern: signups come in, but trial-to-paid conversion isn't where it needs to be. Most of the drop-off is silent. Users sign up, open the product once or twice, and disappear.</p>
    <p>An EEC catches them before that happens.</p>
    <h3 class="mt-4 mb-2">Traffic sources that feed it</h3>
    <p>The EEC landing page gets traffic from the same sources as the trial page. LinkedIn posts by the founder link to it. Blog posts end with it. Paid ads can target it — lower CPA than trial signups because lower commitment. Conference talks mention it.</p>
    <p>The difference: the EEC converts cold traffic that would otherwise bounce.</p>
  </TextBlock>

  <!-- ===== EXPLORE / OFFERINGS ===== -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mb-4">Explore</h2>
      <div class="grid-2 reveal-stagger">
        <LinkCard
          title="Educational Email Courses (EEC)"
          description="The step between 'stranger' and 'trial user.' A 5-7 day course that turns cold traffic into educated subscribers ready for a trial."
          href="/eec/"
        />
        <LinkCard
          title="Behavioral Email Sequences"
          description="Emails triggered by what users actually do during a trial, not by what day it is. For companies with event tracking in place."
          href="/behavioral-emails/"
          badge="In Development"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== AVAILABLE EEC COURSES ===== -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="mb-4 reveal">Available EEC Courses</h2>
      <div class="grid-2 reveal-stagger">
        <LinkCard
          title="From Tool to Platform: 5 Days on What Moves AI SaaS Past the Growth Ceiling"
          description="For founders past product-market fit. Data architecture, trust economics, usage equations, category education, and informational advantage."
          href="/eec/"
          badge="Coming Soon"
        />
        <LinkCard
          title="Mistakes AI SaaS Make"
          description="The basics that quietly determine survival. Wider lens, sharper hooks."
          href="/eec/"
          badge="Coming Soon"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== ARTICLES / LINKEDIN ===== -->
  <TextBlock heading="Articles" alt>
    <div class="grid-2 reveal-stagger">
      <LinkCard
        title="How AI SaaS Differs from Traditional SaaS"
        description="Unique challenges, known solutions on the market."
        href="#"
        badge="Coming Soon"
      />
      <LinkCard
        title="The Reality of AI SaaS"
        description="Processing power, hierarchy, consumer preferences, agentic AI shift."
        href="#"
        badge="Coming Soon"
      />
    </div>
  </TextBlock>

  <!-- ===== NEWSLETTER (legacy — re-enable when link is ready) ===== -->
  <!--
  <TextBlock heading="Newsletter">
    <p>AI SaaS newsletter. Twice a week.</p>
    <a href="https://YOURNEWSLETTERLINK" class="btn btn--primary mt-3">Subscribe</a>
  </TextBlock>
  -->

  <Footer links={footerLinks} />

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .funnel-flow {
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
</style>
